In this game you play 5 different main characters and follow the story of house Forrester during and after the events of the red wedding. This is a story about this noble family trying to survive and preventing it´s house from going in to ruin. As I was playing, this game really made me feel what the characters were going through and I´ve grown so attached to some of them that it really made me feel sad and depressed on some particular moments. That being said, I think this game has a great story (that blends in with the Game of Thrones lore very well) and memorable characters and it is a must have for all the fans of Game of Thrones and the telltale games titles.
I also wanted to give my opinion about the decisions you make in this game. There are many decisions throughout the game that doesn´t change it´s course BUT it changes the WAY you play it and experience it which was always the point in the telltale games and on the other hand there are some decisions that DOES really change on how the story goes and ends and that I´m eager to see it´s impacts on the next Game of Thrones game. So with that in mind, while not perfect, the decisions and consequences that are presented are well made.
Pros:
- Great story and memorable characters;
- TV show voice actors and voice acting is done very well;
- Soundtrack from the show (which we already know it´s really good) and original tracks from the game are also very good (really liked Talia´s song);
- We get to see and experience, from a different angle, some big events that occurs throughout The Game of Thrones show and books (red wedding, the siege of Meereen, etc.);
- 5 playable main characters.
Cons:
- I don´t want to give spoilers but there is a decision early on in the game which it´s outcome doesn´t make sense;
- Graphics could have been better;
- You take 12 hours, approximately, to finish the game.
Overall I really recommend this game. Try to buy it on sale as it is a little expensive for 12 hours of playthrough.
